@model SlideViewModel

<section class="slide-prose">
    <h1>A Calculator Language</h1>
    <h2>(1 + 2) * 3 / -4</h2>

    <p>
        "Math is a language; do what it says," is what my high school math teacher used to say.
        If it's a language, it has grammar and vocabulary. What does that mean?
    </p>

    <p>
        What are our words? Our parts of speech? Our punctuation?
    </p>

    <p>
        Is <strong>4 + -3</strong> valid?<br />
        What about <strong>4+-3</strong>? <strong>+4+-3</strong>?
    </p>

    <p>
        And why are these different?
    </p>

    <p class="expression-examples">
        (1 + 2) * 3<br />
        1 + (2 * 3)<br />
        1 + 2 * 3
    </p>
</section>